# Dashboard API

A Django REST API for serving dashboard metadata backed by a PostgreSQL database.

---

## Prerequisites

Ensure the following are installed before proceeding:

- [Docker Desktop](https://www.docker.com/products/docker-desktop/)
- [pgAdmin 4](https://www.pgadmin.org/download/)
- Python 3 with `pip`

---

## Setup

### 1. Clone the repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/athul-narayanan/dashboardapi
cd dashboardapi
```

### 2. Install Python dependencies

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

### 3. Set up PostgreSQL with Docker

Pull the PostgreSQL image:

```bash
docker pull postgres
```

Start a PostgreSQL container:

```bash
docker run --name dappostgres -e POSTGRES_PASSWORD=Algoma@2024 -p 5434:5432 -d postgres
```

Create the application database:

```bash
docker exec -it dappostgres psql -U postgres -c "CREATE DATABASE dashboarddatabase"
```

### 4. Apply database migrations

Generate migration files:

```bash
python manage.py makemigrations dashboard
```

Apply migrations to the database:

```bash
python manage.py migrate
```

### 5. Connect via pgAdmin 4

Open pgAdmin 4 and create a new server connection using these credentials:

| Field    | Value         |
|----------|---------------|
| Host     | `localhost`   |
| Port     | `5434`        |
| Database | `dashboarddatabase` |
| Username | `postgres`    |
| Password | `Algoma@2024` |

### 6. Seed the database

Run the following SQL in pgAdmin 4 (or via `psql`) to insert sample dashboard records:

```sql
INSERT INTO dashboards (id, type, title, created_time, name, link) VALUES
(1, 'us-senate-election', 'US Senate Election 1967-2022', '2025-04-04', 'Distribution by State and Year',
 'https://public.tableau.com/views/Book3_17425929926010/Sheet1?:language=en-GB&:sid=&:redirect=auth&:display_count=n&:origin=viz_share_link');

INSERT INTO dashboards (id, type, title, created_time, name, link) VALUES
(2, 'us-senate-election', 'US Senate Election 1967-2022', '2025-04-04', 'Total Votes by State',
 'https://public.tableau.com/shared/M5BF4XRNX?:display_count=n&:origin=viz_share_link');

INSERT INTO dashboards (id, type, title, created_time, name, link) VALUES
(3, 'crime', 'Crime Data', '2025-04-04', 'Crime By Region',
 'https://public.tableau.com/views/LearnEmbeddedAnalytics/SalesOverviewDashboard?:language=en-GB&:sid=&:redirect=auth&:display_count=n&:origin=viz_share_link');

INSERT INTO dashboards (id, type, title, created_time, name, link) VALUES
(4, 'crime', 'Crime Data', '2025-04-04', 'Crime Rate By Year',
 'https://public.tableau.com/views/PublicSectorEmployeesCrimeData/CrimeRateByYear?:language=en-GB&:sid=&:redirect=auth&:display_count=n&:origin=viz_share_link');

INSERT INTO dashboards (id, type, title, created_time, name, link) VALUES
(5, 'crime-1', 'Crime Data 1', '2025-04-05', 'Crime Rate By Year',
 'https://public.tableau.com/views/DataAnalysis_17125825841580/CrimeRate?:language=en-GB&:sid=&:redirect=auth&:display_count=n&:origin=viz_share_link');
```

You can add more rows following the same pattern.

### 7. Run the development server

```bash
python manage.py runserver
```

The API will be available at `http://localhost:8000`.

To stop the server, press `Ctrl+C`.

---

## Notes

- Make sure Docker Desktop is running and the `dappostgres` container is active before starting the server.
- The container maps PostgreSQL's default port `5432` to `5434` on your host machine to avoid conflicts with any locally installed PostgreSQL instance.
